      "name": "history-30-audio",
      "question": "Why?",
      "recognizedQuestion": "Y",
      "answer": "CUDA groups threads into warps of 32 so the GPU can issue one instruction across many threads efficiently. If threads in a warp take different branches, each path executes with only its participating lanes active, which can reduce throughput. Modern GPUs support independent thread scheduling, so don’t assume all lanes always execute in lockstep; use explicit synchronization when threads need to coordinate.",
